search teams are literally climbing  mountains to find the black boxes from a  boeing 737 jet that crashed yesterday in  southeastern china  132 people were on that flight and so  far there are no signs of survivors this  is china's first deadly plane crash  since 2010 the boeing jet was just seven  years old seth doan has more on the  story  rescuers in southern china are  continuing to search the hilly rough  terrain where that china eastern  airlines 737 800 crashed after its  nearly vertical nose dive from the sky  this chilling surveillance footage may  have captured the final moments of the  flight this video circulating on social  media has not been verified tracking  data shows the plane departed the  chinese city of kunming early monday and  had been flying at roughly 29 000 feet  before plummeting to 8 000 feet in just  over a minute the aircraft then briefly  climbed about a thousand feet before the  data abruptly ends about 40 seconds  later robert sumwalt is a former  chairman of the national transportation  safety board i think it's very important  to point out that this is not the 737  max that was grounded three years ago  because of two accidents this is the 737  800 which is an earlier model of the 737  it has a very good safety record  crashes during the cruise phase of  flight are reportedly rare is there any  early  idea of what a possible cause might be  well the good thing is is an airplane  like this has has data that is  transmitted on about once every second i  think that the investigators will have a  good idea of what happened  as loved ones wait for answers china  eastern has grounded all of its 737 800s  for cbs morning's seth doan london  my biggest fear the terror that those  people must have experienced on that  plane very very very sorry
 

